course: dictionary
lesson: 10675
title: Unnoticed and the prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unnoticed means not seen, or not paid attention to. The word is built from un- (meaning not) and noticed (seen, or paid attention to), so unnoticed means not noticed.
explain: «The slow loris moves slowly and quietly to sneak up on insects and stay unnoticed.» The clues are slowly, quietly and sneak. The loris wants to be hidden, so unnoticed must mean not seen.
explain: Kind deeds can go unnoticed too. «Her hard work went unnoticed.» Nobody paid attention to her hard work or thanked her for it. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "Her hard work went not paid attention to" is awkward, so try "Her hard work went without anyone noticing it" and see if that fits.
fact: Unnoticed means not seen or noticed by anyone.
fact: Something that goes unnoticed is not paid attention to.
fact: The prefix un- means not, as in unhappy, unlock and unnoticed.
fact: Useful phrases: go unnoticed, pass unnoticed, slip away unnoticed.
fact: «A good day to bury bad news» is a UK saying for a day when bad news goes unnoticed because something bigger is happening.
exercise: «The slow loris moved so quietly that it stayed unnoticed.» What does unnoticed mean here? | Hungry and tired | Very loud and bright | Eaten by an insect | *Not seen by anyone
exercise: «Her hard work went unnoticed.» What does this tell us? | *Nobody paid attention to her hard work | Her hard work was very loud | She stopped working | Everybody cheered her hard work
exercise: Find and copy the word from «The slow loris moves slowly and quietly to sneak up on insects» that shows the loris is trying to stay hidden. | *sneak | loris | slowly | insects
exercise: Which word in «The loris is a small primate from Asia with huge eyes» is the opposite of small? | Asia | primate | eyes | *huge
test: «Dad's birthday card slipped away unnoticed under the sofa.» What does unnoticed mean? | Sent to a friend | Very bright and shiny | *Not seen or paid attention to | Opened very quickly
test: In «A good day to bury bad news», what does it mean for bad news to go unnoticed? | Everyone shouts about the bad news on the radio | *People hardly pay attention to it because something bigger is happening | The bad news is buried under the ground
exam: Which word is the opposite of unnoticed? | Tiny | Careless | *Noticed | Sleepy
